## Slice 3: Channel Pages + Subscriptions

### 12. Subscription routes had swapped param mappings

**Symptom:** Caught during review, before it caused a live bug.

**Root cause:** `subscription.routes.js` mapped `/c/:channelId` to `getSubscribedChannels` and `/u/:subscriberId` to `getUserChannelSubscribers` — backwards from what each controller function actually expected in `req.params`. `getUserChannelSubscribers` reads `channelId`; `getSubscribedChannels` reads `subscriberId`. The route wiring didn't match.

**Fix:**
```js
router.route("/c/:channelId").get(getUserChannelSubscribers).post(toggleSubscription);
router.route("/u/:subscriberId").get(getSubscribedChannels);
```

**File:** `subscription.routes.js`

**Lesson:** Same root category as bug #9, just at a different layer — always trace param names from route → controller destructuring, don't assume they line up just because the file was written in one sitting.

