### 13. `getUserChannelProfile` was locked behind `verifyJWT`, blocking public channel viewing

**Symptom:** Caught during review — logged-out visitors couldn't view any channel page at all, even though the controller's own aggregation pipeline was already written defensively (`req.user?._id` with optional chaining) to handle an anonymous viewer.

**Root cause:** The route had `verifyJWT` applied, even though channel pages should be public (same category as the original `video.routes.js` blanket-auth issue from Slice 1).

**Fix:**
```js
router.route("/c/:username").get(getUserChannelProfile)  // verifyJWT removed
```
Confirmed the controller's existing `isSubscribed: { $cond: { if: {$in: [req.user?._id, ...]} } }` logic already degrades gracefully to `false` for anonymous viewers — no controller changes needed, only the route.

**File:** `user.routes.js`

