**Root cause:** The initial implementation used `window.confirm()` directly rather than a custom UI component — functional, but visually inconsistent with the app's actual design system.

**Fix:** Built a reusable `ConfirmDialog` component (accepting `title`, `message`, `confirmText`, `cancelText`, `onConfirm`, `onCancel` props) styled to match the app's existing dark theme and button conventions, dismissible via backdrop click or Cancel button. Replaced the `window.confirm()` call in the comment-delete flow with this component.

**File:** New `ConfirmDialog` component (frontend), comment delete flow updated to use it

